@startuml
' Activity diagram — a change on the disk, and every way it can be refused
' Sources: ../../specification/04-security.md (section 1), Rule S-1, Rule P-5

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #333
  ArrowColor #333
}

start
:the page posts a change to /api/…;

partition "the reader" {
  :the origin is checked;
  if (the origin is the reader's own?) then (yes)
    :the token is checked;
    if (the token is the reader's own?) then (yes)
      :the path is resolved;
      if (the path is inside one of the roots?) then (yes)
        :the change is made on the disk;
        :the page is told, and reloads;
        stop
      else (no)
        :refused — "that isn't in one of your folders";
        stop
      endif
    else (no)
      :refused — "that request didn't come\nfrom the reader's own pages";
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :refused — the same reason;
    stop
  endif
}

note right
  S-1: a write needs the reader's own origin
  and the reader's own token. The token is
  minted when the reader starts, so a page
  that was open yesterday cannot write
  today.

  P-5: the reader is the only writer (D5).
  Nothing else writes to the disk.
end note
@enduml
